    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1054">

                <pb facs="0996" n="738" xml:id="pg738"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 841.711/124</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Sweden</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Morris</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stockholm</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-12-14T16:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 14, 1915, 4 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received December 15, 8.30 a. m.</hi>]
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>79. Reported Stockholm and confirmed to me by postal administration that British
                    authorities took from Danish steamer 
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Hellig Olav</hi>
                     and detained in Kirkwall three hundred bags mail destined for Sweden
                    from America. Steamer arrived Copenhagen December 11.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Morris</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
